"\n"
"An illustration of the signal received from it was published in\n"
"Scientific American in 1971, and later in The Cambridge Encyclopedia\n"
"of Astronomy in 1977, where it was seen by Stephen Morris, the\n"
"drummer of Joy Division, and was consequently appropriated by\n"
"Peter Saville for the cover of the band's album \"Unknown Pleasures\".\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pulsar\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PSR_B1919%2B21\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unknown_Pleasures\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Saville_%28graphic_designer%29\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joy_Division\n"
"\n"
"Written by Jamie Zawinski; 2013.\n"
"  "
msgstr ""
"\n"
"PSR B1919+21 (AKA CP 1919) was de eerste pulsar ooit ontdekt:\n"
"een draaiende neutronenster die periodiek een vuurtorenachtig baken "
"uitstraalt.\n"
"\n"
"Een illustratie van het signaal dat ervan werd ontvangen, werd gepubliceerd "
"in\n"
"Scientific American in 1971, en later in The Cambridge Encyclopedia\n"
"van Astronomie in 1977, waar het werd gezien door Stephen Morris, de\n"
"drummer van Joy Division, en werd bijgevolg toegeëigend door\n"
"Peter Saville voor de cover van het album \"Unknown Pleasures\" van de "
"band.\n"
"\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pulsar\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PSR_B1919%2B21\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unknown_Pleasures\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peter_Saville_%28graphic_designer%29\n"
"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joy_Division\n"
"\n"
"Geschreven door Jamie Zawinski; 2013.\n"
"  "

